Hi All,

Is there anyway to simulate correlated traits ("shared genetic variance between traits") for qtl mapping with r/qtl?

Thanks--Funda

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Mon Dec  4 05:52:51 2017
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Mon, 04 Dec 2017 05:52:51 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] simulating correlated traits for qtl mapping with r/qtl?
Message-ID: <g5rN47J326g.35EDQtlXAwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <g5rN47J326g.bvf3wrJIAwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <g5rN47J326g.bvf3wrJIAwAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/g5rN47J326g/m/35EDQtlXAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There's nothing built-in for this.

The way I would do it would be to use sim.cross() with 'model' including all QTL affecting any of the traits.
The output contains a 'qtlgeno' component with the genotypes for each simulated QTL.

Then construct the simulated traits in whatever way you want, separately.

karl

